arate fitted kitchen offers a generous range of cupboards and work surfaces, with a rear-facing window bringing in natural light. Also on this level is a stylish contemporary shower room, complete with a large walk-in shower, rainfall showerhead, vanity storage and a heated towel rail.<br /><br />Upstairs, two genuine double bedrooms give the apartment a welcome sense of separation between its living and sleeping accommodation. The principal bedroom measures approximately 16'3\" x 13'3\" and benefits from extensive fitted wardrobes, while the second double bedroom offers flexibility for guests, sharing or working from home. Both rooms feature characterful sloping ceilings and windows on two sides.<br /><br />For commuters, Norwood Junction station provides direct rail services into London Bridge, making this a convenient base for reaching the City and central London. London Overground’s Windrush line adds further travel options, with connections towards Canada Water, Shoreditch High Street and Highbury & Islington.<br /><br />South Norwood High Street and the surrounding streets offer a range of independent cafés, neighbourhood pubs, restaurants and everyday shopping facilities. For time outdoors, South Norwood Lake and Grounds and South Norwood Country Park provide attractive options for weekend walks, exercise and escaping the bustle of London.<br /><br />With two substantial double bedrooms, a generous reception room and a layout that feels distinctly more spacious than a conventional flat, this appealing South Norwood period conversion deserves an internal viewing. Contact Oaks Estate Agents to arrange your appointment.<br /><br />","keyFeatures":["Spacious two double bedroom split level period conversion","Approximately 839 sq ft / 78 sq m of accommodation","Impressive reception room with space for living and dining","Separate fitted kitchen with generous storage and worktop space","Convenient for Norwood Junction station and London Overground","EPC rating: D"]